Framelift 0111: Takion v20 (Sony's current Remote Play stream protocol).

Source: P5M patches/0052-protocolo-do-mac-takion-v20-botao-preso-fec-e-psn.patch (v20 parts).

- Negotiation: on a PS5, after the Takion connect and before the BIG, the stream connection sends
  TAKIONPROTOCOLREQUEST offering 12 and 20 and waits up to 1 s for the ack. If the console picks
  20 it switches (chiaki_takion_set_version) and does the BIG/BANG key exchange on secp521r1 with
  a 66 byte shared secret; with no ack or another answer it stays on 12 exactly as before.
  ChiakiConnectInfo.disable_takion_v20 skips the request (the bridge sets it after a failed v20
  attempt). Registration/pairing and stored credentials are untouched.
- v20 wire format: an 8 byte extended header (send time us + counter, both u32 BE) after the type
  byte of every non-chunk packet (AV, feedback, congestion, mic); MAC and key_pos move by 8.
  Received send times feed a one-way delay variation line every 10 s (INFO).
- v20 AV parsing: audio FEC count narrowed to 12 bits with a mode nibble (mode 2 translated to the
  v12 layout, mode 1 = one multichannel unit per packet), haptics marker in the low nibble.
- Multichannel audio: the channel count from the packet's type byte reopens the Opus decoder as an
  Opus multistream decoder (layout detected from the first packet); frame_cb then gets N channels.
- Trigger effects (8 extra leading bytes on v20) and pad info (0x1a/0x12 sizes on v20).
- packetstats: 16-bit sequence difference (no 2^64 "lost" on wrap); new chiaki_packet_stats_get_total.
- CHIAKI_VEYRA_TAKION_V20_API marks the patched headers.
Not ported (Veyra doesn't need them or they are diagnostics only): the stuck-button feedback
sender changes (already upstream at the pinned commit: bfbb296, 4382c1c, bc397a7), PSN/holepunch changes,
the RUDP ctrl timeout, the P5M_TAKION_PROBE / P5M_AUDIO_CHANNELS experiments (launch spec
audioSettings, AUDIOSTATE), and P5M's per-packet/per-frame diaries and SO_TIMESTAMP receive path.

Ported from P5M (https://github.com/beecrepaldi-afk/P5M), AGPL-3.0, by beecrepaldi-afk,
which is built on chiaki-ng (https://github.com/streetpea/chiaki-ng) and Chiaki by Florian Märkl.
Adapted for Framelift against chiaki-ng 43728af2e639fecb8a7af1cd68c29820a40de973 (on top of
Veyra's 0002 metadata patch and 0100). P5M patches against chiaki-ng 6547d8ae (2026-07-04)
plus its own series; the pinned commit is 135 upstream commits later. Portuguese comments translated.
License: AGPL-3.0-only (LicenseRef-AGPL-3.0-only-OpenSSL, like the files it changes).

